  "notes": "Source: official UCF CECS 'Bachelor of Science Computer Science 2024-2025 Catalog' four-year plan PDF, transcribed course by course 2026-09-30 from https://advising.cecs.ucf.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/2024-2025-Computer-Science-Four-Year-Plan.pdf (identical copy also hosted at https://advising.cecs.ucf.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/2024-2025-Computer-Science-Four-Year-Plan.pdf). Program name per source: Bachelor of Science, Computer Science (College of Engineering and Computer Science, Orlando FL). Course titles use the plan's wording with standard expansions of abbreviations only; nothing invented. CAVEAT (staleness): this is the 2024-2025 catalog edition, not the current 2026-2027 edition. A 'Bachelor of Science in Computer Science Four-Year Plan 2026-2027' is listed on https://www.cs.ucf.edu/current-students/ but its link resolves to an SSO-gated form and the PDF could not be retrieved; no other official 2026-2027 term-by-term CS sequence is retrievable in full, so catalog_year is set honestly to 2024-2025. Credit math: per-term printed hours sum to 121 (122 if the Year-3-Fall Math Elective is taken at 4 hours instead of 3); the plan sheet states no explicit total; the UCF degree requirement is a minimum of 120 unduplicated semester hours, so total_credits is set to the printed-plan sum (121) to satisfy the credit-sum rule. Student-choice slots carry placeholder codes (GEP-1..5, MATH-ELEC, AREA-ELEC-A..F, MATHSTAT-ELEC, FREE-ELEC-A/B) since the plan does not name specific courses. Placement/prereq notes from the plan footnotes: COP 3223C requires a passing CS Placement Test score (or AP CS A 3+ or COP 2500 C or better); COT 3960 (CS Foundation Exam, 0 credits, required_zero) requires COP 3502C and must be passed within one year of COP 3502C. Individual course prereqs are not listed on the plan, so prereq fields are empty (not invented). No TCCNS codes (Florida institution; TCCNS is a Texas system) and no transfer mappings on the source, so tccns/xfer are empty. 11 terms (8-12 required for a bachelor).",
